# H15i — underflow in all three readers, `inf` / `nan` data text, the leading-zero lexer, and the tuple branch

Worktree `D:\Projects\Camel-wt\h15i-number`, branch `handover/H15i-number-text` (from
`develop`). Everything is in the working tree: no commit, no new branch, no push, no logs in
the tree (build and test logs are under `D:\Temp\h15i`).

The design frame is design principles **5.1** (a literal takes the type of its position; a value
that does not fit is a compile-time error; a value is never cut to fit, and there is no implicit
text/value conversion), language reference **2.5** (the number tokens), **10.6** (a refusal is a
located error that says what is wrong), and the rule that every refusal has a catalogue sentence.

