## 4. Tuple literal argument: the missing branch

`src/compile/gir/builder_control.cpp` had array and struct branches in both
`compositeEntersIn` and `compositeDataInType`, but no tuple branch. A tuple literal at a tuple
parameter therefore never entered the parameter's type; a text element made the whole call
`NoMatchingFunction`. Both functions now take `TypeCode::Tuple` / `TupleData` when the sizes
match and walk the elements in written order with `literalElementInType` /
`elementEntersIn`, using the recorded `Tree::LiteralElement` so a diagnostic points at the
element.

Result:

- `pairSum((1, 2.5))` with `f(t: (f32, f32))` is `3.5` (integer element converted once);
- `pairSum(('1.5', 2.0))` is `SemanticDiag::DeclaredTypeMismatch` at the text element
  (line 10, column 22 in `context_tuple_argument_text.cml`), naming `string` and `float`, not
  `NoMatchingFunction`.

Tests: new `context.tuple_argument_text`; `context.composite_argument` gained the numeric
`pairSum((1, 2.5))` line and expected `3.5`. The declaration-only
`context.tuple_field_text` still passes and still reports at its element.

